<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.8.1: Understanding Inequality Symbols</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00496</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.8.1: Understanding Inequality Symbols</md:title>
    <md:uuid>95f98663-17d7-4c96-8e26-a3fcc83a2d96</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>For questions 1 – 3, match each inequality to the meaning of a symbol within it.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="5314b4a8-9916-43e2-8fe9-b836437b52a5"><problem><para>
      <para>\( h &gt; 50 \)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>less than or equal to</para><para>greater than</para><para>greater than or equal to</para></problem><solution><para>greater than</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is greater than. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Is 25 a solution to any of the inequalities? Which one(s)? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Yes; 25 is a solution to \(30 \geq h\) because 30 is greater than or equal to 25.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#5-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Is 40 a solution to any of the inequalities? Which one(s)? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>No; 40 is not a solution to any of the inequalities because 40 does not make any of the inequalities true when substituted in for \(h\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#6-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Is 30 a solution to any of the inequalities? Which one(s)? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Yes; 30 is a solution to \(30 \geq h\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
